From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] android: install host modules under linux-arm64 on arm64
 hosts

On an arm64 Linux host the build OS is always LinuxMusl, but
pathForInstall only collapsed linux_musl to linux when USE_HOST_MUSL was
set, and mapped Common host modules to x86. Host jars such as signapk.jar
then landed in out/host/linux_musl-x86 while make (HOST_OUT) looked in
out/host/linux-arm64.

Collapse linux_musl to linux whenever musl is the build OS, and use arm64
for Common host modules on arm64 hosts. x86_64 hosts are unchanged:
there BuildOS is LinuxMusl exactly when USE_HOST_MUSL is set.
---
 android/paths.go | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/paths.go b/android/paths.go
index 12d15ad..86574b8 100644
--- a/android/paths.go
+++ b/android/paths.go
@@ -2080,9 +2080,9 @@ func pathForInstall(ctx PathContext, os OsType, arch ArchType, partition string,
 			// instead of linux_glibc
 			osName = "linux"
 		}
-		if os == LinuxMusl && ctx.Config().UseHostMusl() {
+		if os == LinuxMusl && ctx.Config().BuildOS == LinuxMusl {
 			// When using musl instead of glibc, use "linux" instead of "linux_musl".  When cross
-			// compiling we will still use "linux_musl".
+			// compiling we will still use "linux_musl". arm64 build hosts always use musl.
 			osName = "linux"
 		}
 
@@ -2095,6 +2095,10 @@ func pathForInstall(ctx PathContext, os OsType, arch ArchType, partition string,
 		if os.Class == Host && (arch == X86_64 || arch == Common) {
 			archName = "x86"
 		}
+		if os.Class == Host && arch == Common && ctx.Config().BuildArch == Arm64 {
+			// Matches HOST_PREBUILT_ARCH, which is arm64 on arm64 build hosts.
+			archName = "arm64"
+		}
 		partitionPaths = []string{"host", osName + "-" + archName, partition}
 	}
 
